1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
(Episode 1)

2
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,660
Mango shaved ice!

3
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:22,820
Thanks for waiting.

4
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,680
- Enjoy.
- Thank you!

5
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,140
Business is pretty slow.

6
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,240
Odajima.

7
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,440
Where are all the girls in bikinis?

8
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:43,000
How is it?

9
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:44,260
Yeah, it's delicious.

10
00:00:44,261 --> 00:00:46,280
- Not a single one.
- Why is that?

11
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,660
This is Okinawa.

12
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:48,720
It's a resort island.

13
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:51,000
It's nothing like the
mainland. Nothing like it.

14
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,020
Did I just say "the mainland"?

15
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,480
You did.

16
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,980
Guess that makes me a real islander, sa~.

17
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:05,880
Did I use "sa" right?

18
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,340
Who knows.

19
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:09,960
Pun on "sa", huh?

20
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,340
You're getting better at this.

21
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,040
Don't go getting funnier than me!

22
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,480
It was an accident.

23
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,400
My stomach hurts from laughing.

24
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,400
All right, all right, don't cry.

25
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,400
Just dust off the dirty
part, and it's still good.

26
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,220
Watch this.

27
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,400
Whoa...

28
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:45,520
It's full of sand!

29
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,580
You can't eat this!

30
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:47,840
Gross!

31
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,400
- Ugly!
- Huh?

32
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,600
- Ugly! Ugly!
- Handsome! Handsome!

33
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,919
Ugly! Ugly!

34
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,160
Handsome! Handsome! Handsome!

35
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:00,036
Handsome! Handsome!
Handsome! Handsome! Handsome!

36
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:02,200
Say it again! Say handsome!

37
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:05,840
I still think back to it.

38
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,520
Odajima.

39
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,990
Go kill Kataoka.

40
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,100
Killing this man

41
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,700
was once my sole reason for living.

42
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:37,960
Kataoka-san!

43
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,560
- Here.
- Thanks.

44
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:56,780
Take it.

45
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,060
- On the house.
- Thank you!

46
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,460
Yummy!

47
00:03:04,461 --> 00:03:05,819
Good, huh?

48
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,820
Yeah!

49
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,560
Look, an airplane!

50
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:12,799
You like planes?

51
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,800
Uh-huh!

52
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:15,920
Yet here we are.

53
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,040
Side by side,

54
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,800
looking up at the same sky.

55
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:40,920
Thank you so much!

56
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,940
Island men drink after they dance!

57
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,680
I hear ya!

58
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,120
Everyone,

59
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:48,620
cheers!

60
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,870
Yeah! Let's drink up tonight!

61
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:57,940
Cheers!

62
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,240
Odajima.

63
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,040
Have a drink, too.

64
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:13,410
Sure.

65
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:21,700
Excuse me.

66
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,080
I'll have an ice cream soda, please.

67
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:24,299
An ice cream soda? Seriously?!

68
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,740
Coming right up! One ice cream soda!

69
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,180
You told me to get a drink.

70
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,780
You're such a buzzkill.

71
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:35,870
A stiff bastard like you
needs a drink to loosen up.

72
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:39,520
Listen. The only things that
should be hard in this world

73
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,280
are rice crackers

74
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,260
and "that thing."

75
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,400
That thing?

76
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:46,540
Really?

77
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:47,580
Damn straight.

78
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,800
You know, "that thing."

79
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,760
Hey.

80
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,000
Sorry to keep you waiting.

81
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,280
Odajima.

82
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,100
Yes?

83
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,700
Let me have a sip later.

84
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,800
Sure.

85
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:09,320
Boss, thanks for always taking care of us.

86
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,860
- Thank you, Boss!
- I told you, I'm not your boss anymore.

87
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,819
How's work at the restaurant?

88
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:18,060
We're just part-timers, but
we basically run the place.

89
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,219
I've gotten real good at
making mozuku tempura!

90
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,560
Oh, not bad at all.

91
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:24,680
- Keep it up.
- Yes, sir! Back to work!

92
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,039
Handsome! One more order of sea grapes!

93
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,480
Right away! One order of sea grapes!

94
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:34,480
Look at those two.

95
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:37,160
They were just petty
punks when we first met.

96
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:39,380
Take us with you!

97
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,760
- Exactly!
- Boss!

98
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,460
- Pull over!
- Don't leave us behind!

99
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Boss!

100
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,040
To think we retired,

101
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,960
and they still chased us
all the way to Okinawa.

102
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:56,420
It's getting late.

103
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,680
- Time to head back.
- Understood.

104
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:00,900
We're taking off.

105
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,660
Kataoka, see you next time.

106
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,720
Aya-chan, that was a wonderful song.

107
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,540
Thank you.

108
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:07,119
- Come back soon!
- Sure, see you later.

109
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:08,120
See you.

110
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:09,960
Thanks for having us.

111
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,580
The night breeze feels nice.

112
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:23,060
It's been three years since the
boss took us in here in Okinawa.

113
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:27,400
Twenty years in the
yakuza, and I never knew.

114
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,520
An honest day's work,

115
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,460
dinner after sundown,

116
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,380
and a good drink.

117
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:38,280
A life like this...

118
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,380
I guess this is what happiness feels like.

119
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:49,500
You don't need to stand
guard over me anymore.

120
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,340
You can have a drink, too.

121
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,020
You noticed?

122
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,540
It's a curse, being in
the yakuza for so long.

123
00:06:59,226 --> 00:07:00,946
Can't shake years of conditioning.

124
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,520
No matter how much I
drink, I can't even get buzzed.

125
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:08,540
Still...

126
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,860
I'd kind of like to see you drunk.

127
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:13,820
Right.

128
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:16,630
How about downing a
bottle of Awamori next time?

129
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:18,020
No thanks.

130
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:20,820
Come on, such a party pooper.

131
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,660
Then Habushu it is.

132
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:25,180
I hear it gets you rock hard.

133
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,280
Where?

134
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:29,380
Where?

135
00:07:30,886 --> 00:07:31,886
Down "there."

136
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,080
A life like this...

137
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,160
is what happiness feels like.

138
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:29,270
Kill me.

139
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:42,390
Kill me.

140
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:44,840
- Kill me!
- You think you can escape?

141
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,299
You're just like me.

142
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,680
You will never...

143
00:08:47,730 --> 00:08:51,150
never find happiness.

144
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:19,740
I can never be happy.

145
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,520
I don't deserve happiness.

146
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:30,240
(Kumakura: Kataoka-san, please
contact me as soon as possible.)

147
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,420
- Hey, get up!
- Please!

148
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,170
Don't kill me!

149
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:52,300
Spare my life!

150
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,800
Shut up!

151
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:57,840
I'm telling the truth!

152
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,540
Please, believe me!

153
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,000
All your screaming made me die in the game.

154
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
I'm begging you!

155
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:11,740
Have mercy!

156
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:24,260
Chairman.

157
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,200
Tell me.

158
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:29,360
Do you know the difference
between "shameless" and "brazen"?

159
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,760
No...

160
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:33,500
I'm not an educated man,

161
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,100
so I wouldn't know.

162
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:37,840
Being "brazen"...

163
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,960
Even if someone oversteps,

164
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,960
somehow you can't completely hate them.

165
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,280
However,

166
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:47,390
being "shameless" is just pure greed,

167
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,500
or downright deceitful.

168
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,340
Ah.

169
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,360
Is it because "shameless"
means without shame?

170
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,480
So you see,

171
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:05,260
cooking the books and
then begging for your life...

172
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,560
Isn't that utterly shameless?

173
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,600
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

174
00:12:19,490 --> 00:12:20,730
Morning, Kataoka.

175
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:22,490
We're back again today!

176
00:12:23,730 --> 00:12:25,850
I bet you're not getting
any shaved ice today either.

177
00:12:31,730 --> 00:12:33,949
- Excuse me.
- Welcome!

178
00:12:33,950 --> 00:12:34,950
Welcome!

179
00:12:37,970 --> 00:12:39,370
- Here.
- Oh, no...

180
00:12:40,230 --> 00:12:41,230
Um...

181
00:12:41,430 --> 00:12:44,050
Can I buy a phone charger around here?

182
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,000
- A charger?
- Yes.

183
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:56,610
You can borrow mine.

184
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,020
Really? Are you sure?

185
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:00,370
Thank you so much!

186
00:13:01,710 --> 00:13:02,710
Are you here alone?

187
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:07,310
Shin-chan, he's letting us borrow his!

188
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:11,680
Thank you.

189
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,930
- Is that your girl, kid?
- Yes.

190
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:17,930
And actually,

191
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:19,890
we're getting married soon.

192
00:13:23,170 --> 00:13:24,870
- That's on the house.
- Huh?

193
00:13:25,530 --> 00:13:26,530
Really...?

194
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:28,070
Take good care of her, all right?

195
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:31,060
Thank you, sir!

196
00:13:32,950 --> 00:13:34,229
He's so nice.

197
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,230
Yeah.

198
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:37,490
He told you to cherish me.

199
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:39,710
I will. I promise.

200
00:13:41,430 --> 00:13:42,430
Odajima.

201
00:13:47,110 --> 00:13:48,230
Where are all the customers?

202
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:51,910
Not a single one.

203
00:13:53,190 --> 00:13:54,390
Boring.

204
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:00,450
Strange.

205
00:14:00,770 --> 00:14:01,770
Where did my phone go?

206
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:19,200
(Kumakura: Kataoka-san, please
contact me as soon as possible.)

207
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,620
Here.

208
00:14:32,650 --> 00:14:33,650
Say ahh.

209
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,920
We're so slow today.

210
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:46,630
Right this way.

211
00:14:58,450 --> 00:14:59,450
Pardon the intrusion.

212
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:01,370
My apologies.

213
00:15:01,590 --> 00:15:04,510
The Chairman is out, so I'll
be meeting with you instead.

214
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,400
I appreciate it.

215
00:15:07,130 --> 00:15:08,130
What brings you here?

216
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:11,010
Ihashi-san.

217
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:14,590
Regarding this month's tribute payment...

218
00:15:19,070 --> 00:15:20,270
Is there a problem with it?

219
00:15:21,150 --> 00:15:22,150
Well...

220
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:24,930
Would it be possible

221
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:27,110
to give us a few extra days?

222
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:31,330
Is this what the Fourth Leader wants?

223
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:32,890
No.

224
00:15:36,270 --> 00:15:37,490
This is on my own accord.

225
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,450
That's problematic.

226
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:43,390
Matters like this must be discussed
with the Fourth Leader in person.

227
00:15:45,130 --> 00:15:46,490
So, Kumakura-san,

228
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:50,530
make sure the payment is made on time.

229
00:15:56,730 --> 00:15:57,830
If, by chance,

230
00:15:58,750 --> 00:15:59,950
it happens to be late...

231
00:16:08,970 --> 00:16:09,970
Understood.

232
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,840
Oh, and another thing.

233
00:16:19,236 --> 00:16:22,994
The Chairman asked me to
convey that the Fourth Leader

234
00:16:23,018 --> 00:16:26,426
should attend executive
meetings once in a while.

235
00:16:36,610 --> 00:16:37,610
It's me.

236
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:40,710
What's the status on the revenues
from our Awakuma territory?

237
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:44,870
Cut the crap and scrape up the cash now!

238
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:51,920
Boss...

239
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:57,050
Our profits are falling
short of expectations.

240
00:16:59,710 --> 00:17:02,340
We're running out of working capital.

241
00:17:02,370 --> 00:17:03,790
(Two Major Bottlenecks in Awakuma)

242
00:17:05,130 --> 00:17:06,430
We're short on cash...

243
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:11,510
"Evaluation pending
due to public safety risks."

244
00:17:13,290 --> 00:17:15,090
"Investment decisions suspended."

245
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,850
Kataoka, we're taking off.

246
00:17:26,030 --> 00:17:26,670
Thanks again.

247
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:29,809
- Get home safe.
- Kataoka, we'll be back tomorrow!

248
00:17:29,810 --> 00:17:31,930
All right. Make sure to buy
some shaved ice tomorrow!

249
00:17:32,770 --> 00:17:33,970
Look at you grinning.

250
00:17:37,470 --> 00:17:38,810
About time to close up.

251
00:17:41,350 --> 00:17:42,350
Hm?

252
00:17:42,890 --> 00:17:45,450
Odajima?

253
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:48,250
Yes.

254
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:14,010
You've been acting weird all day.

255
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:18,090
Hey.

256
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:37,410
Come to think of it, we got married,
but we never had a ceremony.

257
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:39,590
Huh?

258
00:18:41,430 --> 00:18:43,270
What kind of wedding would you want?

259
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:34,390
(Kumakura: Apologies for reaching out repeatedly.
Please get back to me as soon as possible.)

260
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:39,530
Is that my phone?

261
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:45,010
Huh?

262
00:19:51,930 --> 00:19:52,930
This is Kumakura.

263
00:19:54,150 --> 00:19:55,570
If things continue like this,

264
00:19:57,650 --> 00:19:59,690
the Kirii-gumi will be
wiped out by the Koutokukai.

265
00:20:01,690 --> 00:20:02,890
I know you've retired,

266
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:06,010
and I have no right to beg you.

267
00:20:07,530 --> 00:20:08,730
But Kataoka-san,

268
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:10,070
to save the Kirii-gumi,

269
00:20:11,250 --> 00:20:12,350
I beg of you,

270
00:20:12,930 --> 00:20:14,030
please come back.

271
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:42,030
Why did you hide this from me?

272
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:46,890
I'm deeply sorry.

273
00:21:00,590 --> 00:21:01,590
I'm truly

274
00:21:02,530 --> 00:21:03,530
sorry.

275
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:19,410
I keep having

276
00:21:22,770 --> 00:21:23,970
the exact same dream.

277
00:21:29,570 --> 00:21:31,070
I see the man I killed.

278
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:37,060
He tells me, "Don't think you can escape."

279
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:41,590
"You will never find happiness."

280
00:21:47,190 --> 00:21:48,190
Waking up.

281
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,180
Working.

282
00:21:53,230 --> 00:21:54,230
Eating.

283
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,510
Sleeping in the same bed.

284
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:01,250
Living like normal people,

285
00:22:02,630 --> 00:22:03,830
spending each day with you.

286
00:22:07,570 --> 00:22:08,890
Even after paying a massive price

287
00:22:11,810 --> 00:22:13,610
to break ties and buy my freedom,

288
00:22:16,410 --> 00:22:17,410
I still feel like

289
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:19,450
I can't go anywhere at all!

290
00:22:23,610 --> 00:22:24,610
So, Kataoka-san,

291
00:22:27,810 --> 00:22:28,810
at least for you...

292
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:34,250
I wanted at least for you to live freely.

293
00:23:17,810 --> 00:23:18,910
You idiot.

294
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,550
You're far too stiff.

295
00:23:35,570 --> 00:23:37,110
Not that I dislike that about you.

296
00:23:41,630 --> 00:23:42,630
Listen, Odajima.

297
00:23:46,690 --> 00:23:47,690
We

298
00:23:50,430 --> 00:23:51,430
are free.

299
00:23:54,150 --> 00:23:56,270
It's because we're free that
we can choose not to be.

300
00:23:57,190 --> 00:23:59,470
Isn't clinging to freedom
just another form of restraint?

301
00:24:01,270 --> 00:24:02,350
Odajima.

302
00:24:04,230 --> 00:24:05,430
We are free.

303
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:10,590
We can do anything,

304
00:24:13,230 --> 00:24:14,630
and go anywhere.

305
00:24:18,510 --> 00:24:19,510
Odajima.

306
00:24:25,070 --> 00:24:26,070
What is it

307
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:30,090
that you truly desire?

308
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:35,600
Freedom...

309
00:25:16,750 --> 00:25:17,750
All right.

310
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:19,560
Let's go.

311
00:25:26,190 --> 00:25:27,290
What's wrong, Odajima?

312
00:25:29,210 --> 00:25:30,210
Nothing.

313
00:25:30,750 --> 00:25:31,750
It's fine.

314
00:25:35,150 --> 00:25:37,190
You didn't forget the phone, did you?

315
00:25:41,190 --> 00:25:42,190
Kataoka-san.

316
00:25:42,850 --> 00:25:44,030
Yeah? What is it?

317
00:25:45,130 --> 00:25:46,130
That's not just a phone.

318
00:25:46,310 --> 00:25:47,310
It's a smartphone.

319
00:25:58,030 --> 00:25:59,030
Hey.

320
00:25:59,590 --> 00:26:01,116
How long are we supposed to watch the shop?

321
00:26:01,140 --> 00:26:02,610
How should I know, idiot?

322
00:26:04,190 --> 00:26:07,620
Probably until the Boss gets back.

323
00:26:09,290 --> 00:26:11,570
Not like there are any customers anyway.

324
00:26:13,550 --> 00:26:14,550
Tell me about it.

325
00:26:22,130 --> 00:26:23,130
Chairman.

326
00:26:23,650 --> 00:26:24,970
The Kirii-gumi's payment...

327
00:26:26,090 --> 00:26:27,290
I'm afraid it will be delayed.

328
00:26:33,190 --> 00:26:34,490
Pulling a stunt like this...

329
00:26:35,670 --> 00:26:37,630
How do they plan to settle it?

330
00:26:46,390 --> 00:26:47,390
How

331
00:26:47,450 --> 00:26:48,450
will

332
00:26:48,610 --> 00:26:49,610
they

333
00:26:50,190 --> 00:26:51,190
settle

334
00:26:51,250 --> 00:26:52,250
this?

335
00:27:18,750 --> 00:27:19,950
It's been so long.

336
00:27:20,970 --> 00:27:22,070
This familiar sensation.

337
00:27:26,430 --> 00:27:27,530
And now,

338
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:30,940
the real show begins.

339
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:39,990
(Next Episode Preview)

340
00:27:40,030 --> 00:27:41,550
Three years later,

341
00:27:41,950 --> 00:27:43,230
I'm back.

342
00:27:43,254 --> 00:27:44,254
Hell.

343
00:27:44,650 --> 00:27:45,950
Our pride is our lifeblood.

344
00:27:46,250 --> 00:27:48,610
Even the Boss will be
devoured if he shows weakness.

345
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:50,290
At this rate,

346
00:27:50,550 --> 00:27:52,270
the Koutokukai will wipe us out completely.

347
00:27:52,580 --> 00:27:54,210
Don't tell me

348
00:27:54,370 --> 00:27:56,590
you're blushing seeing me in a suit?

349
00:27:56,650 --> 00:27:58,030
Good. Excellent.

350
00:27:58,830 --> 00:28:00,790
Brazen enough. I love it.

351
00:28:01,090 --> 00:28:02,650
What will you do if I get taken?

352
00:28:03,140 --> 00:28:05,150
Next time, I'll protect you no matter what.

353
00:28:06,590 --> 00:28:07,990
Hey, Odajima!
